WEBVTT

00:01:28.413 --> 00:01:30.538
And when the cortisol levels increase,

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:32.788
electrical signaling
in your hippocampus,

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:37.246
this part of your brain that is related
to learning, memory, and stress control,

00:01:37.288 --> 00:01:38.746
deteriorates.

00:01:38.996 --> 00:01:42.163
The hippocampus also blocks
the activity of the HPA axis,

00:01:42.204 --> 00:01:43.454
so when it weakens,

00:01:43.496 --> 00:01:46.996
your ability to control
stress weakens too.

00:01:47.454 --> 00:01:48.746
But that’s not all.

00:01:49.038 --> 00:01:53.079
In fact, cortisol can reduce
the size of your brain.

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:58.704
Too much cortisol can cause the loss
of synaptic connections between neurons

00:01:58.746 --> 00:02:01.704
and the shrinking
of your prefrontal cortex,